        'Start with the location in the example. The words “the old well” name a landmark, and “beside” uses that whole group to tell where Inez stopped. If you replace the landmark with “the gate”, you get another location with the same structure.\n\nSyntax studies both the order of words and the way they group. Putting “the” after “well” breaks the word order. Drawing all the words as branches at the same level loses the grouping. The inner brackets show the landmark, and the outer brackets show where the landmark fits inside the location. This arrangement of groups within groups is called hierarchy.',
