        'First ask whether the bracketed clause supplies content or describes a group named by a noun. In the first sentence, “that the gate jammed” tells what the claim was. In the second, “that Vic made” identifies which claim and has a gap where the object of “made” would go.\n\nThe third sentence also has an object gap, but the relative supplies a separate comment about the already identified NP “her claim”. Use the gap to find the relatives and use the intended reference to tell the restrictive and non-restrictive readings apart. Then decide which level each clause joins in a tree.',
